ion":{"id":19877,"exampleId":5670,"difficulty":2}},{"id":62272997,"studentId":57975,"choices":null,"selectedChoice":1,"selectId":0,"correct":1,"timeElapsed":15897,"question":{"id":79305,"exampleId":5670,"difficulty":2}}],"completedStr":"Completed @ 2:20 PM","exampleAnswers":[{"id":9520,"number":1,"title":"Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form","answers":[{"id":62272810,"created":"2026-10-15T14:17:48.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12608,"number":1,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 2:17 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":124490,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":9520,"text":"<p>Which of the following is equivalent to $(k-1)!$ for any $k \\geq 4?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(k-1) \\cdot (k-2) \\cdot (k-3)!$","choice2":"$(k-1) \\cdot (k-2) \\cdot (k-3)$","choice3":"$(k-1) \\cdot (k-2) \\cdot \\: \\cdots \\: \\cdot4$","choice4":"$(k-1) \\cdot (k-3)!$","choice5":"$(k-1) \\cdot (k-2)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Using the definition of factorial, we have </p>\n<p>\\[\n(k-1)! = (k-1) \\cdot (k-2) \\cdot (k-3) \\cdot (k-4) \\cdot \\: \\cdots \\: \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Now, applying the factorial definition to all but the first two factors, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n(k-1)! \n&= (k-1) \\cdot (k-2) \\cdot \\overbrace{{\\color{blue} (k-3) \\cdot (k-4) \\cdot \\: \\cdots \\: \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1 }}^{\\large (k-3)!} \\\\[5pt]\n&= (k-1) \\cdot (k-2) \\cdot {\\color{blue}(k-3)!}\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":3710,"name":"Factorials in Variable Expressions"},"example":{"id":9520,"title":"Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form"},"group":{"id":16440,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242842,"answer":{"id":62272810,"cread":"2026-10-15T14:17:48.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12608},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62272826,"created":"2026-10-15T14:18:06.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14685,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 2:18 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":124492,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":9520,"text":"<p>Which of the following is equivalent to $(n-2)!$ for any $n \\geq 4?$</p>\n","choice1":"$(n-2) \\cdot (n-3) \\cdot (n-4)!$","choice2":"$(n-2) \\cdot (n-3) \\cdot (n-4)$","choice3":"$(n-2) \\cdot (n-4)!$","choice4":"$(n-2) \\cdot (n-3)$","choice5":"$(n-2) \\cdot (n-3)\\cdot \\: \\cdots \\: \\cdot 4$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Using the definition of factorial, we have</p>\n<p>\\[\n(n-2)! = (n-2) \\cdot (n-3) \\cdot (n-4) \\cdot (n-5) \\cdot \\: \\cdots \\: \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Now, applying the factorial definition to all but the first two factors, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n(n-2)! \n&= (n-2) \\cdot (n-3) \\cdot \\overbrace{{\\color{blue}(n-4) \\cdot (n-5) \\cdot \\: \\cdots \\: \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1}}^{\\large (n-4)!} \\\\[5pt]\n&= (n-2) \\cdot (n-3) \\cdot {\\color{blue}(n-4)!}\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":3710,"name":"Factorials in Variable Expressions"},"example":{"id":9520,"title":"Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form"},"group":{"id":16440,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242842,"answer":{"id":62272826,"cread":"2026-10-15T14:18:06.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14685},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":5669,"number":2,"title":"Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient of Factorials","answers":[{"id":62272853,"created":"2026-10-15T14:18:29.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14840,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 2:18 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":122060,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":5669,"text":"<p>Given that $n \\geq 2$ is an integer, simplify $\\dfrac{(n-2)!(n+1)!}{(n!)^2}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$\\dfrac{n+1}{n(n-1)}$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{n(n+1)}{n-1}$","choice3":"$\\dfrac{n^2-1}{n}$","choice4":"$\\dfrac{1}{n(n-1)}$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{1}{n(n+1)}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, notice the following:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\nn! &= n \\cdot (n-1) \\cdot (n-2)! \\\\[3pt]\n(n+1)! &= (n+1) \\cdot n!\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Then, we cancel the $(n-2)!$ and $n!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{(n-2)!(n+1)!}{(n!)^2} & = \\dfrac{(n-2)!(n+1)!}{n!\\cdot n!}\\\\[5pt]\n\n& = \\dfrac{(n-2)!\\cdot  (n+1) \\cdot n!}{n!\\cdot n \\cdot (n-1) \\cdot (n-2)!}\\\\[5pt]\n\n& = \\dfrac{\\cancel{(n-2)!}\\cdot  (n+1) \\cdot \\cancel{n!}}{\\cancel{n!}\\cdot n \\cdot (n-1) \\cdot \\cancel{(n-2)!}}\\\\[5pt]\n\n& = \\dfrac{n+1}{n(n-1)}\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":3710,"name":"Factorials in Variable Expressions"},"example":{"id":5669,"title":"Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient of Factorials"},"group":{"id":81643,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242842,"answer":{"id":62272853,"cread":"2026-10-15T14:18:29.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":4,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14840},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62272891,"created":"2026-10-15T14:18:43.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":9608,"number":4,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 2:18 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:10","question":{"id":122049,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":5669,"text":"<p>Given that $n \\geq 0$ is an integer, simplify $\\dfrac{(n+3)!}{n!}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)$","choice2":"$\\dfrac1{(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)}$","choice3":"$n(n+2)(n+3)$","choice4":"$(n+2)(n+3)$","choice5":"$(n+1)(n+2)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, notice the following:\n\\[\n(n+3)! = (n+3) \\cdot (n+2) \\cdot (n+1) \\cdot n!\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we cancel the $n!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\\begin{align}\n\\require{cancel}\n\\dfrac{(n+3)!}{n!} & = \\dfrac{ (n+3) \\cdot (n+2) \\cdot (n+1) \\cdot n!}{n!}\\\\[5pt]\n\n& = \\dfrac{ (n+3) \\cdot (n+2) \\cdot (n+1) \\cdot \\cancel{n!}}{\\cancel{n!}}\\\\[5pt]\n\n& = (n+1)(n+2)(n+3)\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":3710,"name":"Factorials in Variable Expressions"},"example":{"id":5669,"title":"Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient of Factorials"},"group":{"id":81642,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242842,"answer":{"id":62272891,"cread":"2026-10-15T14:18:43.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":9608},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62272914,"created":"2026-10-15T14:19:02.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14994,"number":5,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 2:19 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":73023,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":5669,"text":"<p>Given that $n \\geq 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\dfrac{(n+1)!}{(n-1)!}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$n(n+1)$ ","choice2":"$n^2(n+1)$ ","choice3":"$n(n-1)$ ","choice4":"$(n-1)(n+1)$ ","choice5":"$n(n-2)$ ","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, notice the following:</p>\n<p>\\[\n(n+1)! =(n+1)\\cdot  n \\cdot (n-1)!\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we cancel the $(n-1)!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{(n+1)!}{(n-1)!} & = \\dfrac{(n+1)\\cdot  n \\cdot (n-1)!}{(n-1)! }\\\\[5pt]\n\n& = \\dfrac{(n+1)\\cdot  n \\cdot \\cancel{(n-1)!}}{\\cancel{(n-1)!}}\\\\[5pt]\n\n& = n(n+1)\n\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":3710,"name":"Factorials in Variable Expressions"},"example":{"id":5669,"title":"Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient of Factorials"},"group":{"id":81642,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242842,"answer":{"id":62272914,"cread":"2026-10-15T14:19:02.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14994},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":5670,"number":3,"title":"Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient With Many Factorials","answers":[{"id":62272934,"created":"2026-10-15T14:19:26.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14819,"number":6,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 2:19 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":19882,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":5670,"text":"<p>Given that $n \\geq 9$ is an integer, simplify $\\dfrac{(n-8)!\\, (n+9)!}{(n-9)!\\, (n+7)!}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$(n-8)(n+8) (n+9)$","choice2":"$(n+7)(n+8) (n+9)$","choice3":"$\\dfrac{n+9}{n-9}$","choice4":"$(n+8) (n+9)$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{(n+8) (n+9)}{n-9}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, we notice that\n\\begin{align*}\n(n+9)! &= (n+9)(n+8)(n+7)!\\\\[3pt] \n(n-8)! &= (n-8)(n-9)! \n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Then, we can cancel the $(n+7)!$ and $(n-9)!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\t\\require{cancel}\n\n\t\t\\dfrac{(n-8)!\\, (n+9)!}{(n-9)!\\, (n+7)!} &= \\dfrac{ [(n-8) \\cdot (n-9)!] \\cdot [(n+9) \\cdot (n+8) \\cdot (n+7)!]}{(n-9)! \\cdot (n+7)!}\\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{ (n-8) \\cdot \\cancel{(n-9)!} \\cdot (n+9) \\cdot (n+8) \\cdot \\cancel{(n+7)!}}{\\cancel{(n-9)!} \\cdot \\cancel{(n+7)!}}\\\\[5pt]\n\t&= (n-8) \\cdot (n+8) \\cdot (n+9) \\\\[5pt]\n&=(n-8)(n+8) (n+9)\n\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":3710,"name":"Factorials in Variable Expressions"},"example":{"id":5670,"title":"Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient With Many Factorials"},"group":{"id":81645,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242842,"answer":{"id":62272934,"cread":"2026-10-15T14:19:26.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14819},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62272977,"created":"2026-10-15T14:19:45.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13362,"number":7,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 2:19 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":19877,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":5670,"text":"<p>Given that $k \\geq 0$ is an integer, $\\dfrac{\\left ((k+1)!\\right)^2}{k!}=$</p>\n","choice1":"$(k+1)^2 k!$","choice2":"$(k+1)^2$","choice3":"$\\dfrac{(k+1)^2}{ k!}$","choice4":"$\\dfrac{k+1}{ k!}$","choice5":"$(k+1) k!$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, we notice that\n\\[\n(k+1)! = (k+1)k! \n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we can cancel the $k!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\t\\require{cancel}\n\t\t\\dfrac{\\left( (k+1)!\\right)^2}{k!} & = \\dfrac{\\left( (k+1) k!\\right)^2}{k!}  \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{ (k+1)^2\\, \\cdot(k!)^2}{k!}\\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{ (k+1)^2\\, \\cdot k!\\cdot \\cancel{k!}}{\\cancel{k!}}\\\\[5pt]\n\t&=(k+1)^2 k!\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":3710,"name":"Factorials in Variable Expressions"},"example":{"id":5670,"title":"Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient With Many Factorials"},"group":{"id":81644,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242842,"answer":{"id":62272977,"cread":"2026-10-15T14:19:45.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13362},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62272997,"created":"2026-10-15T14:20:05.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15897,"number":8,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 2:20 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":79305,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":5670,"text":"<p>Given that $m \\geq 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\dfrac{(m+2)!}{(m+2)\\ (m-1)!}=$</p>\n","choice1":"$m^2+ m$","choice2":"$m^2$","choice3":"$m^2+m+1$","choice4":"$\\dfrac{m+1}{m}$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{m}{m+1}$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>First, we notice that\n\\[\n(m+2)! = (m+2)(m+1)(m)(m-1)! \n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we can cancel the $(m+2)$ and $(m-1)!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\require{cancel} \n\\dfrac{(m+2)!}{(m+2)\\ (m-1)!} &= \\dfrac{(m+2)\\cdot (m+1)\\cdot m \\cdot (m-1)! }{(m+2) \\cdot (m-1)!}\\\\[5pt]\n\n& =\\dfrac{\\cancel{(m+2)}\\cdot (m+1)\\cdot m \\cdot \\cancel{(m-1)!} }{\\cancel{(m+2)} \\cdot \\cancel{(m-1)!}}\\\\[5pt]\n\n& = (m+1) \\cdot m\\\\[5pt]\n\n& =m^2 + m\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":3710,"name":"Factorials in Variable Expressions"},"example":{"id":5670,"title":"Simplifying a Variable Expression Containing a Quotient With Many Factorials"},"group":{"id":81644,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242842,"answer":{"id":62272997,"cread":"2026-10-15T14:20:05.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15897},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]}],"localGraph":{"topicId":3710,"topics":[{"id":371,"name":"Multiplying Binomials","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":8.57983681339539,"repetition":3,"stability":0.36319738697731313},{"id":423,"name":"Simplifying Rational Expressions by Factoring","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":1483.4994178023053,"repetition":10,"st